meta {
  name: Renewal Outreach Desk
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/crm/service-tickets/renewals/desk
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  ~X-Branch-Id: {{branchId}}
}

tests {
  test("returns 200 OK", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });

  test("returns an array of desk rows", function () {
    expect(res.getBody()).to.be.an("array");
  });

  test("every row carries the fields the desk renders", function () {
    for (const row of res.getBody()) {
      expect(row).to.have.property("cycleId");
      expect(row).to.have.property("ticketId");
      expect(row).to.have.property("stepKey");
      expect(row).to.have.property("label");
      expect(row).to.have.property("clientName");
      expect(row).to.have.property("renewalDate");
      expect(row).to.have.property("daysUntilRenewal");
      expect(row).to.have.property("daysUntilAvailable");
      expect(row).to.have.property("isActionable");
      expect(row).to.have.property("isOverdue");
      expect(row.policies).to.be.an("array");
    }
  });

  test("daysUntilAvailable is null exactly when the call is actionable", function () {
    // The one invariant the UI depends on: it gates the Start button on this
    // rather than comparing `availableAt` to the browser clock.
    for (const row of res.getBody()) {
      expect(row.daysUntilAvailable === null).to.equal(row.isActionable);
    }
  });

  test("previewed calls are within the preview window and not yet open", function () {
    for (const row of res.getBody()) {
      if (row.daysUntilAvailable === null) continue;
      expect(row.daysUntilAvailable).to.be.at.most(14);
      expect(row.isActionable).to.equal(false);
      expect(row.isOverdue).to.equal(false);
      expect(row.status).to.equal("waiting");
    }
  });

  test("actionable rows sort ahead of previewed ones", function () {
    const rows = res.getBody();
    let seenScheduled = false;
    for (const row of rows) {
      if (row.daysUntilAvailable !== null) seenScheduled = true;
      else expect(seenScheduled).to.equal(false);
    }
  });

  test("one row per cycle", function () {
    const ids = res.getBody().map((row) => row.cycleId);
    expect(new Set(ids).size).to.equal(ids.length);
  });
}

docs {
  # GET /crm/service-tickets/renewals/desk

  The **Proactive Renewal Outreach** desk on the Service Dashboard
  (`/crm/service`): one row per open renewal cycle, flattened to the single call
  that is on the CSR's plate — plus the calls about to land on it.

  - **Module:** `crm_service`
  - **Permission:** `crm_service:read`
  - **Data scope:** applied as everywhere else. A cycle whose call is not
    visible to the caller simply produces no row, so an `own`-scoped CSR sees
    the calls assigned to them rather than the agency's whole book.

  ## ⚠ This read has a side effect

  Reading the desk runs the throttled renewal scan first
  (`materializeRenewalCycles`), which is what creates cycles and their call
  tickets. **There is no cron** — this request is what makes newly-due renewals
  appear. A first call against a fresh database can therefore be slow and can
  return rows that did not exist a moment earlier.

  ## Params

  None.

  ## Response

  `RenewalDeskRow[]` — see `@sfa/shared` `service/renewal.ts`. Sorted:
  actionable calls first (overdue ahead of the rest, then soonest renewal),
  then previewed calls by how soon they open.

  Capped at the 100 soonest-renewing incomplete cycles.

  ### Previewed calls (the `daysUntilAvailable` field)

  Every other list in the CRM hides a call until its `availableAt`
  (`scheduledStepMatches` keeps them out of the queue and the KPI strip) — a
  call that has not opened is not work. **This desk is the deliberate
  exception:** it is the one surface whose job is the coming fortnight, and a
  T-45 call first appearing on the morning it opens cannot be planned around.

  Calls opening within `RENEWAL_DESK_PREVIEW_DAYS` (**14**) are returned with:

  | field | previewed call | call on the plate |
  |---|---|---|
  | `daysUntilAvailable` | whole days until it opens (`0` = today) | `null` |
  | `isActionable` | `false` | `true` |
  | `status` | `waiting` | `open` / `overdue` |

  `daysUntilAvailable` is the flag to gate UI on — computed against the
  **server clock** and shipped as a number, for the same reason `isActionable`
  is. A browser that re-derived it from `availableAt` could offer a Start
  button that `POST …/renewals/steps/:stepKey/complete` then rejects with a
  400, since that endpoint independently refuses a step before its
  `availableAt`.

  An **open call always wins its cycle's row.** Both calls of an annual cycle
  can be in range at once — an annual review still open at T-50 beside a
  renewal review opening at T-45 — and previewing the later one while the
  earlier is unfinished would bury real work.

  ### What is deliberately absent

  No premium-change field. `Policy.premium` is a single current number and the
  system holds no premium history, so an increase cannot be computed; the desk
  shows the renewal window and the call, nothing invented.

  ## Errors
  | Status | When |
  |---|---|
  | 401 | Missing/expired bearer token |
  | 403 | `crm_service` disabled for the agency, or the caller lacks `crm_service:read` |
}
